-- Migration 10: a session records the build that recorded it.
--
-- The sidecar carried a hand-maintained `app_version` string that no build system agreed with, so
-- "which build produced this recording?" had no answer. That is now `build_id`, generated from the
-- single `monad.version` property, and for a session that ends through stop() the running build can
-- simply fill it in.
--
-- An *interrupted* session cannot: its sidecar is assembled by a later launch, which may be a
-- different build entirely, and stamping the recovering build's identity onto the recording build's
-- data would be a quiet lie about provenance. So the identity is persisted at open() instead, and
-- recovery reads it back.
--
-- Additive and nullable: a row written by an earlier build simply has NULL here, which reads as
-- "this build could not say" rather than as a wrong answer.
ALTER TABLE LabSessionRecord ADD COLUMN buildId TEXT;
